PDF fragments
description: a page number and a rectangle in the page's own units
- >
  A **PDF fragment** names a **page** (counted from 1) and a rectangle on it: `x`, `y` from the
  page's top-left corner, in the page's own units (points, the size the page reports at scale 1),
  so the stored region is independent of the viewer's zoom:
- !!<format: text/x-yamlover> |
  type: pdf
  page: 12
  x: 72
  y: 540
  w: 180
  h: 36
- >
  The fragment also embeds a PNG crop of the region ([the crop sidecar](*::annotations:fragments:crop)).
